ROLE: systems_reviewer  VOTE: yellow
PROMPT_VERSION: v001
EXISTING_IMPLEMENTATIONS: [
  {system: "RouteLLM", url: "https://github.com/lm-sys/RouteLLM ; https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.18665", overlap: "Pre-generation strong/weak model routing with calibrated cost threshold; overlaps with cascade/routing structure, but routes by generic query difficulty/preference, not predicted quantization degradation."},
  {system: "FrugalGPT", url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.05176", overlap: "LLM cascade for cost/quality tradeoff; overlaps with cheap-to-expensive escalation, but not quantization-sensitivity-specific and not a serving-engine mixed-precision mechanism."},
  {system: "SGLang sgl-router", url: "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/tree/main/experimental/sgl-router", overlap: "Shipping/OSS OpenAI-compatible router with round_robin/random/power_of_two/cache_aware_zmq policies; no evidence of quantization-degradation-aware routing."},
  {system: "vLLM quantization + mixed precision", url: "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/main/docs/features/quantization/quark.md", overlap: "Supports quantized and layerwise mixed-precision models such as MXFP4/FP8 and unquantized layers; this is static/model/layer precision selection, not per-request pre-decode full-vs-quant routing."},
  {system: "TensorRT-LLM quantization / mixed precision checkpoints", url: "https://github.com/NVIDIA/TensorRT-LLM/blob/main/examples/quantization/README.md", overlap: "Supports FP8/INT4_AWQ/GPTQ/full_prec and MIXED_PRECISION per-layer checkpoint formats; no found request-level router predicting quantization degradation."},
  {system: "FlashInfer / LMCache", url: "https://github.com/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer ; https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache", overlap: "Provide quantization kernels / KV-cache infrastructure; searched code showed kernels/cache routing, not request-level quant-sensitivity routing."}
]
CONTRIBUTION_TYPE: mechanism
SCALE_REALISM: "Does not yet hold at realistic workload: EXP-0020 is L0 synthetic trace simulation with latent s_i-generated degradation, not real 4-bit GPTQ/AWQ vs full outputs on real prompts. No serving-system throughput, batching, queueing, GPU memory residency, KV-cache, or FLOPs/$ accounting. Reproducibility of the artifact is reasonable for the toy claim because PREREG.md, sim.py, and CSVs are listed, but reproducibility of the systems claim is insufficient until L1 measures real per-request degradation distribution, pre-decode AUC, post-decode confidence baseline, and end-to-end serving cost."
RATIONALE: "No exact OSS implementation was found in vLLM/SGLang/LMCache/FlashInfer/TensorRT-LLM for pre-decode routing based specifically on predicted quantization sensitivity. However, the surrounding mechanism is mostly known: RouteLLM/FrugalGPT already do strong/weak LLM routing for cost-quality, and vLLM/TensorRT-LLM already support quantized and mixed-precision models. The only possible systems content is the quantization-degradation-specific pre-decode signal. EXP-0020 does not establish that signal in a real system: AUC 0.77-0.89 and router-conf gains up to about 0.024 quality come from a synthetic latent model; at low noise the confidence cascade ties it with CI including 0. Therefore this is not yet a systems insight/design result; it is a plausible mechanism requiring real-model validation."
